From b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare Browser <noreply@localhost>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 23:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 72/73] Add in-browser task manager and memory saver

Brings Chromium Desktop's Task Manager and memory inspector to Android:

- Live process and tab memory table: Inspect individual renderer processes, PIDs,
  and exact RAM usage (MB) per tab directly within the browser settings.
- Traffic light memory indicator: Color-coded visual status badge (Green <80MB,
  Yellow 80-250MB, Red >250MB) for quick readability.
- Granular Process Control: End individual renderer processes or put background
  tabs to sleep (discard) to free up memory without losing tab URLs.
- Thermal and Battery Optimized Polling: Polling runs exclusively while the Task
  Manager screen is open and active, pausing immediately on exit.
- Two update modes: 'Calculate only on open' (zero background overhead) or
  'Live update in real-time' (1.5s refresh intervals while viewing).
- Configurable Auto-Discard: Automatically puts background tabs to sleep after
  inactivity to prevent memory exhaustion on low-memory devices.
